    <span class="vcaSectionLabel">Our People</span>
    <h2 class="vcaSectionTitle">The people behind the journey</h2>
    <p class="vcaSectionText">The guides, hosts, growers, artists and storytellers who make the Virunga experience possible.</p>
    <div class="vcaPeopleGrid">
<article class="vcaPerson"><span>Founder & Concierge</span><h3>Fabrice</h3><div class="vcaPersonOrigin"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> Musanze Base</div><p>“10+ years designing private cultural and wilderness journeys across Rwanda, Uganda, and DRC.”</p></article>
<article class="vcaPerson"><span>Master Tracker</span><h3>Gervais</h3><div class="vcaPersonOrigin"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> Kinigi Headquarters</div><p>“Deep generational instinct tracing mountain gorilla families through the bamboo mist.”</p></article>
<article class="vcaPerson"><span>The Grower</span><h3>Jean-Pierre</h3><div class="vcaPersonOrigin"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> Mount Bisoke Slopes</div><p>“Cultivates award-winning Bourbon coffee cherries on mineral-rich volcanic high slopes.”</p></article>
<article class="vcaPerson"><span>The Hearth</span><h3>Claudine</h3><div class="vcaPersonOrigin"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> Virunga House Hearth</div><p>“Brings the highland harvest alive over open wood fires with fragrant traditional recipes.”</p></article>
<article class="vcaPerson"><span>The Artist</span><h3>Innocent</h3><div class="vcaPersonOrigin"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> Musanze Arts Quarter</div><p>“Shapes volcanic earth and banana leaf fibers into timeless cultural expressions.”</p></article>
